de'}, {'parameter': 'instanceLocation', 'value': 'JsonNodePath.root()'}, {'parameter': 'walk', 'value': 'false'}], 'expected': 'Set containing one ValidationMessage with messageKey "oneOf.indexes" and arguments "3, 0, 1, 2" (all three schemas are valid).', 'description': 'Three schemas are valid, canShortCircuit() returns false, therefore the loop iterates over all schemas and the validator reports a OneOf error listing all three matching indexes.'}]}, {'group': 'No discriminator – no schema matches', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'executionContext', 'value': 'mock ExecutionContext with failFast=true, discriminator disabled, reportChildErrors=true, canShortCircuit=true'}, {'parameter': 'node', 'value': 'invalid JsonNode (e.g., {"a":"string"})'}, {'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': 'same as node'}, {'parameter': 'instanceLocation', 'value': 'JsonNodePath.root()'}, {'parameter': 'walk', 'value': 'false'}], 'expected': 'Set containing one ValidationMessage with messageKey "oneOf" and argument "0" (zero valid schemas). Child errors from each schema are also present in the returned set.', 'description': 'All schemas return non‑empty error sets. reportChildErrors() is true, so child errors are collected. Since numberOfValidSchema == 0, a OneOf error with count 0 is produced together with the child errors.'}]}, {'group': 'Discriminator enabled – matching discriminator property', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'executionContext', 'value': 'mock ExecutionContext with failFast=false, discriminator enabled, canShortCircuit=true, reportChildErrors=false, DiscriminatorContext active'}, {'parameter': 'node', 'value': 'JsonNode {"type":"A"}'}, {'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': 'same as node'}, {'parameter': 'instanceLocation', 'value': 'JsonNodePath.root()'}, {'parameter': 'walk', 'value': 'false'}], 'expected': 'empty Set – validation succeeds (discriminator matches $ref of the only valid schema, numberOfValidSchema == 1, no errors).', 'description': 'Discriminator keyword is enabled. The parent schema contains a discriminator validator with propertyName "type" and mapping {"A":"#/components/schemas/A"}. The node contains "type":"A" which matches the $ref of the first schema, causing the discriminator context to mark a match. Because a match is found, no discriminator‑related error is emitted and the OneOf rule is satisfied.'}]}, {'group': 'Discriminator enabled – discriminator present but no matching $ref', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'executionContext', 'value': 'mock ExecutionContext with failFast=false, discriminator enabled, canShortCircuit=true, reportChildErrors=false, DiscriminatorContext active'}, {'parameter': 'node', 'value': 'JsonNode {"type":"B"}'}, {'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': 'same as node'}, {'parameter': 'instanceLocation', 'value': 'JsonNodePath.root()'}, {'parameter': 'walk', 'value': 'false'}], 'expected': 'Set containing one ValidationMessage with messageKey "oneOf" and argument "0" AND a discriminator‑specific message: "based on the provided discriminator. No alternative could be chosen based on the discriminator property".', 'description': 'Discriminator is enabled, the node contains the discriminator property but its value does not correspond to any $ref in the candidate schemas. The discriminator context does not mark a match, so after the loop the validator adds the special discriminator error and then the generic OneOf error (since numberOfValidSchema == 0).'}]}, {'group': 'Discriminator enabled – discriminator property missing (ignore path)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'executionContext', 'value': 'mock ExecutionContext with failFast=false, discriminator enabled, canShortCircuit=true, reportChildErrors=false, DiscriminatorContext active'}, {'parameter': 'node', 'value': 'JsonNode {} (no discriminator property)'}, {'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': 'same as node'}, {'parameter': 'instanceLocation', 'value': 'JsonNodePath.root()'}, {'parameter': 'walk', 'value': 'false'}], 'expected': 'Set containing one ValidationMessage with messageKey "oneOf" and argument "0" (no valid schemas). No discriminator‑specific error because the context is marked as ignore.', 'description': 'The discriminator property is absent; the discriminator context marks IGNORE. Consequently the validator does not emit the special discriminator‑no‑match message. Since no schemas validate, a normal OneOf error with count 0 is returned.'}]}, {'group': 'Walk flag true – schema validation via walk()', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'executionContext', 'value': 'mock ExecutionContext with failFast=false, discriminator disabled, reportChildErrors=false, canShortCircuit=true'}, {'parameter': 'node', 'value': 'valid JsonNode that passes walk() of first schema only'}, {'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': 'same as node'}, {'parameter': 'instanceLocation', 'value': 'JsonNodePath.root()'}, {'parameter': 'walk', 'value': 'true'}], 'expected': 'empty Set – one schema validates via walk(), numberOfValidSchema == 1, no errors.', 'description': 'When the walk flag is true the validator calls schema.walk() instead of schema.validate(). The mock schema returns an empty set, leading to a successful OneOf validation.'}]}, {'group': 'Discriminator disabled – child errors collected when reportChildErrors true', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'executionContext', 'value': 'mock ExecutionContext with failFast=false, discriminator disabled, reportChildErrors=true, canShortCircuit=false'}, {'parameter': 'node', 'value': 'invalid JsonNode (fails both schemas)'}, {'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': 'same as node'}, {'parameter': 'instanceLocation', 'value': 'JsonNodePath.root()'}, {'parameter': 'walk', 'value': 'false'}], 'expected': 'Set containing one ValidationMessage with messageKey "oneOf" (count 0) and also the child ValidationMessages from both schemas (unioned).', 'description': 'Discriminator is off, but reportChildErrors() returns true, so the validator must collect the error sets from each failing schema and include them together with the final OneOf error.'}]}]
